<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends flat vs dollar in dull trade.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends flat vs dollar in dull trade.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka closed unchanged at 42.3800/42.3900 to the dollar in interbank trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the market was mostly quiet because of the weekend closure of most international markets. &quot;There was hardly any dealing today,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>Dealers said the interbank call money rates closed up at 4.5-5.2 percent against the previous 4.0-4.75 percent.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom 880-2-506363</p>
